WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.305
Five teams want machine learning this quarter.

2
00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:05.005
Pick the right tool for each,

3
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:08.905
then put one model into production and keep it healthy.

4
00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:11.840
The rule: the least effort that meets the need.

5
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.128
If Google already solves the task, call the API.

6
00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:19.575
Vision, Natural Language, Speech, Translation, Document AI.

7
00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:21.450
Your own labels and no coders?

8
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:22.388
AutoML.

9
00:00:22.408 --> 00:00:24.550
Data in BigQuery and a SQL team?

10
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.235
BigQuery ML.

11
00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:27.660
Full control of the model?

12
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.660
Custom training on Vertex AI.

13
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.823
Training hardware.

14
00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:33.647
CPUs for small models.

15
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.045
GPUs for most deep learning.

16
00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:42.055
TPUs for huge models full of matrix multiplications, with no custom operations.

17
00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.292
If the GPUs sit idle, fix the input pipeline.

18
00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:47.965
TFRecord files and prefetching.

19
00:00:47.985 --> 00:00:52.590
To tune hyperparameters, Vertex AI uses Bayesian optimization.

20
00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.490
Fewer trials than a grid search.

21
00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.852
An online endpoint answers one request in milliseconds.

22
00:00:58.872 --> 00:01:00.650
You pay while it runs.

23
00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.660
Batch prediction scores millions of rows offline, then stops.

24
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.798
A feature store gives training and serving the same features.

25
00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:09.635
No skew.

26
00:01:09.655 --> 00:01:12.495
Models get worse as the world changes.

27
00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:15.245
Skew: serving data differs from training data.

28
00:01:15.265 --> 00:01:18.405
Drift: serving data changes over time.

29
00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:21.130
A pipeline retrains on old and new data,

30
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.580
and deploys only if the new model is better.

31
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.840
Recap.

32
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.078
Least effort wins.

33
00:01:27.098 --> 00:01:28.928
TPUs for huge models.

34
00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:30.378
Batch when nobody waits.

35
00:01:30.398 --> 00:01:32.425
Monitor, then retrain.

36
00:01:32.445 --> 00:01:35.220
Try the checkpoint below.
